# CAR with theta_0 = -30 (PV1_2), LONPOLE = 150 and CRVAL2 = -30.00000001:
# the native pole lands 1.2e-8 deg from the celestial pole and celset's
# z = cos(latp) cos(lat0) = 1.75e-10 is just ABOVE its 1e-10 tolerance, so
# wcslib takes the general atan2 branch for the native pole's longitude
# (cel.c), which here differs by 1.2e-4 deg (0.42 arcsec) from the
# "celestial north pole at the native pole" shortcut. A z tolerance looser
# than 1.75e-10 takes the shortcut and fails. Synthetic.
NOTE pipeline: celset z = 1.75e-10, just above the 1e-10 tolerance
GRID 1 512 9 1 512 9
SKYGRID 0 350 8 -80 80 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CTYPE1  = 'RA---CAR'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--CAR'
CRVAL1  = 10.0
CRVAL2  = -30.00000001
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CDELT1  = -0.1
CDELT2  = 0.1
PV1_2   = -30.0
LONPOLE = 150.0
LATPOLE = 90.0
